<!-- ================================================================= -->
<!--  Chapter 4: Cleaning and Recoding Data                            -->
<!--                                                                    -->
<!--  Opens with the West Africa Ebola outbreak (2014-2016), drawing on -->
<!--  two real, verified papers:                                       -->
<!--    - Owada et al. (2016), Frontiers in Public Health 4:163           -->
<!--      (Sierra Leone national surveillance data problems)            -->
<!--    - Roshania et al. (2016), Global Health: Science and Practice   -->
<!--      4(3), 394-409 (IMC's multicountry clinical data collection)   -->
<!--  Then a real worked example from this course's own STACK question  -->
<!--  bank (tracker ID 76, "missing values 1" - crop grown/sold/profit  -->
<!--  data, Moodle entryid=108891), narrated from the tracker's review  -->
<!--  comments rather than invented numbers, since the live STACK XML   -->
<!--  has not been exported into assets/stack/ yet - see the comment    -->
<!--  below sec-stack-crop-example for what to do once it is.           -->
